{"title":"Career roadmap · Weather Analyst","role":"Weather Analyst","summary":"A Weather Analyst studies atmospheric conditions and weather data to produce forecasts, warnings, climate assessments and operational insights. The work combines meteorology, atmospheric physics, mathematics, statistics, satellite data, radar, numerical weather prediction and programming.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Meteorology / Atmospheric Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observations","Quality Control","Atmospheric Analysis","Numerical Models","Satellite/Radar Data","Forecast","Verification","Communication"]},{"type":"p","text":"A Weather Analyst may work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weather forecasting"},{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"Agriculture/weather services"},{"text":"Marine meteorology"},{"text":"Disaster and severe-weather monitoring"},{"text":"Energy forecasting"},{"text":"Climate analytics"},{"text":"Environmental monitoring"},{"text":"Research and atmospheric modelling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career, although many professional meteorologist and specialist analyst positions prefer a master's degree in Meteorology, Atmospheric Science, Physics, Mathematics or a closely related field."},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Sc. Meteorology / Atmospheric Science"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Weather Analyst"},{"type":"flow","items":["Atmospheric Science","Meteorology","Weather Forecasting"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct/near-direct"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Weather Analyst, Meteorological Analyst, Weather Forecaster Trainee, Forecasting Assistant, Meteorological Data Analyst, Atmospheric Research Assistant"},{"type":"note","label":"Assumption","text":"three/four-year B.Sc. structure depending on the university, beginning in 2026."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build atmospheric physics, mathematics, statistics, programming, weather observation and forecasting fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter weather/meteorological analysis or pursue M.Sc. specialisation in atmospheric science, meteorology or related quantitative fields."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Weather Analyst, Forecasting Specialist, Numerical Weather Prediction or specialised meteorology roles."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward Lead Meteorologist, Forecasting Manager, Atmospheric Scientist, Research Scientist or specialised weather-intelligence leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Mathematics, physics and atmospheric fundamentals"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Atmospheric-science fundamentals project"},{"text":"Quantitative foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Thermodynamics, fluid mechanics and Earth systems"},{"text":"NPTEL + university labs"},{"text":"Atmospheric thermodynamics report"},{"text":"Physics foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Meteorology, atmospheric dynamics and weather observation"},{"text":"NPTEL + meteorological resources"},{"text":"Weather-observation log"},{"text":"Meteorological capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Synoptic meteorology, clouds, precipitation and severe weather"},{"text":"NPTEL + weather datasets"},{"text":"Synoptic weather analysis"},{"text":"Forecasting capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Numerical methods, statistics, Python and data analysis"},{"text":"Python + NPTEL"},{"text":"Weather-data analysis project"},{"text":"Computational capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Satellite, radar, GIS and numerical weather prediction"},{"text":"NASA Earthdata","url":"https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/"},{"text":"Satellite/radar analysis"},{"text":"Operational capability"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Sem 1"},{"text":"Forecast verification, modelling and specialised forecasting"},{"text":"Research/internship"},{"text":"Forecasting case study"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Sem 2"},{"text":"Dissertation + meteorological internship + PG/job preparation"},{"text":"Research institute/meteorological organisation"},{"text":"Forecasting portfolio"},{"text":"Career readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"h","text":"Atmospheric science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atmospheric Physics"},{"text":"Physical Meteorology"},{"text":"Dynamic Meteorology"},{"text":"Synoptic Meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Atmospheric Chemistry"},{"text":"Climatology"},{"text":"Cloud Physics"},{"text":"Radiation"},{"text":"Boundary-Layer Meteorology"},{"text":"Tropical Meteorology"},{"text":"Mesoscale Meteorology"},{"text":"Weather Systems"},{"text":"Severe Weather"},{"text":"Climate Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative foundation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Differential Equations"},{"text":"Linear Algebra"},{"text":"Vector Calculus"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Numerical Methods"},{"text":"Fluid Mechanics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"MATLAB"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Scientific computing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Weather-analysis skills"},{"type